# enscribe — what git deliberately does not track.
#
# Written to the repo's actual needs, not from a generic boilerplate. Two
# generated files are deliberately committed; this file is written to not
# match them (see "Do NOT ignore" at the bottom).

# ─── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# npm-workspaces hoists most deps to the root `node_modules/`, but per-package
# `node_modules/` directories also appear (e.g. the enscribe package holds a
# per-package `.package-lock.json`). The unscoped `node_modules/` pattern (no
# leading slash) matches at every level.
node_modules/

# ─── Build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tsup-built browser library (packages/enscribe/dist/) is a
# generated, minified bundle, reproducible via `npm run build:lib`. Unlike the
# two generated files deliberately committed (see bottom), it is NOT tracked: it
# is large, machine-built, and rebuilt on demand. The `dist/` pattern (no
# leading slash) matches the per-package dist directory at any depth — and does
# not match either committed `src/` file below, nor anything under `site/` (the
# built site writes to the `-o` ROOT, not a `dist/` subdir).
dist/

# ─── THIS site's build output (docs-source/ → site/) ────────────────────────
# `site/` is the built docs site (enscribe.org). It is a deploy fact of THIS repo
# only: the STATIC build writes to `site/` (home at the root), the portable LIVE
# folder to `site/live/`. The engine's output is purely `-o`-driven and knows
# nothing of these paths. The built tree is deliberately COMMITTED so GitHub Pages
# serves it with no build step; rebuild with `npm run build:site-all` (which does
# `rm -rf site` first — a clean rebuild, never additive staleness). Committed build
# output is an accepted tradeoff: the tree can lag `docs-source/` until the next
# rebuild + commit (or until CI automates it).
#
# The ONE exception (the same rationale the retired `site/dist/` rules carried,
# repointed to the new layout): the STATIC pages are self-contained — they inline
# their CSS, with no local <link>/<script> — so the large machine-built engine
# assets copyShellAssets drops at the static root are UNUSED there, the same ~3 MB
# bundles the `dist/` policy keeps untracked everywhere else. They are ignored at
# the static root ONLY. The LIVE folder's copies (site/live/*) ARE referenced by
# the live shell and stay tracked; the leading-slash paths below anchor to the
# static root, so they never match site/live/.
/site/enscribe.browser.global.js
/site/enscribe-shell.css
/site/editor-codemirror.js
/site/default.css

# ─── Working prompt files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `ghc-prompt-*.md` files are crafted prompts the user pastes into the repo
# root while running a slice; they are working scratch, never artifacts to
# commit.
ghc-prompt-*.md

# ─── WSL / Windows download-metadata ────────────────────────────────────────
# WSL preserves NTFS alternate-data-stream markers as `*.Zone.Identifier`
# files when prompt files are downloaded from a Windows browser. Mild cruft.
*.Zone.Identifier

# ─── Do NOT ignore (deliberately committed generated files) ─────────────────
# Two files in this repo are build-generated but deliberately committed —
# `git status` should always show them as part of the project, and any
# `.gitignore` change here that quietly starts matching them is a bug:
#
#   packages/layer1-vocabulary/src/data.js
#     The Layer 1 vocabulary data module, generated from elements/*.md by
#     packages/layer1-vocabulary/build/generate-data-module.js. Committed per
#     the Slice 4 Phase 0's Option-A ruling (committed + pretest
#     regenerate-and-diff staleness guard). See notes/specs/core.md.
#
#   packages/enscribe/src/parser/generated/parser.js
#     The Peggy-generated parser, produced from grammar/enscribe.peggy by
#     packages/enscribe/build/compile-grammar.js. Committed so the
#     parser package is consumable without a build step at install time.
#
# The patterns above are deliberately narrow (node_modules/, ghc-prompt-*.md,
# *.Zone.Identifier) and do not match either path. If you add a broader
# pattern below — anything matching `**/*.js` or `**/generated/**` or `**/src/data.*` —
# add an explicit unignore here so the deliberate files stay tracked, e.g.:
#   !packages/layer1-vocabulary/src/data.js
#   !packages/enscribe/src/parser/generated/parser.js
.claude/worktrees/
*:Zone.Identifier
*:Zone.Identifier
